Contract: `ApplyBatch` is all-or-nothing. If any row in the batch cannot be written, no row from that batch may remain applied. The storage API has no implicit transaction. The implementation is:

```go
type Store interface {
    Put(Row) error
}

func ApplyBatch(s Store, rows []Row) error {
    for _, row := range rows {
        if err := s.Put(row); err != nil {
            return err
        }
    }
    return nil
}
```

Does this meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.
